  "description": "Register, sign in and sign out for a Rask app, on by default. Accounts are backed by ASP.NET Core Identity (versioned password hashing, lockout, security stamps) and exposed through Rask's own host-neutral surface — the same IUserProvider, Authorize component and [Authorize] routes work unchanged on the Server, WebAssembly, island, SPA and meta-framework hosts. Ships built-in overridable /login, /register and /logout pages plus the matching /api/auth endpoints, so a TypeScript front end gets the same flows. Email confirmation and password reset go out through the app's own mail queue, with /confirm-email, /forgot-password and /reset-password pages to match. The first account to register becomes the admin.",
